code, the old stomping ground of the David

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:07.660
Pakman show.

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:09.690
Who's calling today from four one three.

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:10.830
Hello? Yes.

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:13.110
Can you hear me?

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:14.110
Yes.

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:16.400
Hi, this is Mike kin from Western mass.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:17.990
Hey Mike, what's up?

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:26.580
So, um, I just have some questions about,
um, your position on health care.

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:27.580
Okay.

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:34.620
So, um, a lot of the progressive media has
been saying that, you know, TYT or secular

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:40.690
talk or other media have been saying that
Bernie's Medicare for all Virgin Vernon's

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:43.500
version is the populous position.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:50.980
But if you look at the polls, um, it's actually,
um, the Medicare for all who wanted, or the

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:56.489
public option, which is the popular position.

00:00:56.489 --> 00:01:01.920
Sorry, did you get cut off or was, was there
a question there?

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:03.140
Yeah, sorry.

00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:04.780
Yeah, I got cut off.

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:11.330
So my question is, what's your position on,
what's your position on Medicare for all specific,

00:01:11.330 --> 00:01:17.930
specifically Bernie's position because, um,
according to the polls, the apocalypse position

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:20.920
is Medicare for all who want it?

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:22.100
The public option.

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:25.890
I don't know what, what do you, according
to the polls, what, what does that mean?

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:28.870
According to the polls, the popular, popular
or popular list?

00:01:28.870 --> 00:01:31.509
I'm having a really hard time understanding
what you're saying.

00:01:31.509 --> 00:01:32.509
Okay.

00:01:32.509 --> 00:01:33.509
Pop folk.

00:01:33.509 --> 00:01:37.439
Well, I guess popular position is um, public
corruption.

00:01:37.439 --> 00:01:38.439
Okay.

00:01:38.439 --> 00:01:42.820
I've not seen those polls and the polls have
nothing to do with what I think would be best.

00:01:42.820 --> 00:01:44.270
So here's the deal.

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:47.869
The public option is a milk toast half measure.

00:01:47.869 --> 00:01:53.479
The best studies I've seen say that if you
pass a public option, it will reduce premiums

00:01:53.479 --> 00:01:55.160
by about 7%.

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:58.770
And of course premiums often go up by 10%
every year.

00:01:58.770 --> 00:02:03.680
So it would basically save part of one year's
increase in premiums.

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:05.859
It's a very milk toast half measure.

00:02:05.859 --> 00:02:10.810
It doesn't really fix the problems we have
Medicare for all fixes.

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:13.330
Lots of the problems that we have.

00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:14.349
There are some issues.

00:02:14.349 --> 00:02:15.560
No plan is perfect.

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:20.680
There are some issues with Medicare for all,
uh, one of them being that, uh, the, the best

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:28.700
studies I've seen say in order to really deliver
the care quality level at the accessibility

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:33.360
level that Bernie wants, that it's simply
going to cost way more than he says.

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:34.430
That might still be okay.

00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:35.430
Right?

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:37.959
Like we might say, it'll cost way more, but
that's okay.

00:02:37.959 --> 00:02:42.310
Um, but yeah, I mean, as the polls you're
citing, I haven't seen them.

00:02:42.310 --> 00:02:44.720
I, I don't know anything about that.

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:46.060
Okay.

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:51.980
So let's say that hypothetically because you
didn't see it, let's say that it is a public

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:58.629
option is the most popular position among
the general population, but you still want

00:02:58.629 --> 00:03:02.330
to push for Bernie's version of Medicare for
all.

00:03:02.330 --> 00:03:07.909
Uh, so my view on this is not informed by
what people like, I mean, listen, 60 something

00:03:07.909 --> 00:03:09.560
million people voted for Donald Trump.

00:03:09.560 --> 00:03:11.480
It happened to be fewer than the number that
voted for Hillary.

00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:14.920
But like I, I don't really care about it being
popular or unpopular.

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:20.549
My view is what do the studies say about how
to deliver the best care most effectively

00:03:20.549 --> 00:03:22.019
to the most number of people.

00:03:22.019 --> 00:03:26.250
And the public option is just, it's just a
half measure and it won't do very much.

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:27.489
Oh, okay.

00:03:27.489 --> 00:03:28.740
All right.

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:31.230
Thanks for the answer.

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:32.230
I appreciate that.

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:33.590
All right, Mike, great to hear from you.

00:03:33.590 --> 00:03:36.950
Great to hear from folks in, uh, in, in Western
Massachusetts.

